# Prettier scope.
#
# Principle: at M1, formatting governs the code this milestone creates. It does
# NOT retroactively reformat the repository. Running `prettier --write .` across
# everything touched 41 pre-existing files — the whole M0 spike, the 2000-line
# roadmap, and the promoted capability spec — which is unrelated churn that would
# bury this milestone's actual change in a reformat diff. Each exclusion below
# records why that file is not governed.

# Generated and machine-written.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Installed skill content is generated. AGENTS.md forbids editing it by hand, and
# reformatting it would create a diff against its upstream source of truth.
.agents/

# The M0 measurement harness. It is disposable, is not a workspace member, is
# governed by its own contract and self-test, and has established formatting that
# a reformat would obscure when it is eventually retired.
tests/provider-spike/

# OpenSpec workflow output. Specs and change artifacts have their own authored
# formatting, and the promoted specs in openspec/specs/ are the behavioural
# source of truth — reformatting their bytes is churn with no benefit.
openspec/

# Long-form pre-existing documents, each with established formatting across
# thousands of lines. Reformatting them would produce a diff unrelated to any
# change. New documents created by this milestone are NOT excluded.
AGENTS.md
docs/ROADMAP.md
docs/PROVIDERS.md
